# An allowlist (packaging): the image needs only the locked runtime requirements
# (requirements-runtime.txt; requirements.txt adds the test runner), the source and the dashboard's
# source.
# Everything else stays out of the build context: tests, tooling, docs, .git, .claude, the
# virtualenv, coverage output and any .env file. The upload allowlist is a separate contract,
# kept in scripts/package-appstore.sh, and scripts/smoke-container.sh builds from that upload
# artefact rather than the working tree, so untracked files never reach a release image.
*
!requirements-runtime.txt
!src/
!frontend/
# `!src/` and `!frontend/` re-admit whole subtrees, so these are excluded again inside them,
# including any environment file (.env, .env.*, .env-*, .envrc, *.env), and the dashboard's
# local dependencies, build output and coverage, which the image rebuilds from the lockfile.
**/.env*
**/*.env
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage
src/app/static
# The dashboard's tests and their helpers: the image builds the dashboard, never tests it.
frontend/src/**/*.test.ts
frontend/src/**/*.test.tsx
frontend/src/test
